⟦ vos_package_readme_standard | STANDARD-v1 | vsm-1.2.1 | 2026-08-29T01:10:00Z ⟧

@vsm 1.2.1
@status active

// STANDARD for the README/docs of EVERY vOS package — public OR private.
// Derived from the reference quality of `socratic-engine` and `state-canon-mcp`
// (rmw3, 2026-08-29). The user directive: same rigor for ALL repos. A public
// instrument must read like those two.
//
// Companion to voslab_directory_tree_proposal.vsm + voslab_packaging_proposal.vsm.

required_sections() {
  badges: "CI · Python 3.10+ · License · MCP / dependencies (where relevant)"
  tagline: "> one-line philosophy quote (the bet in a sentence)"
  status: "honest current state — built / tested / roadmap; no proclaimed claims"
  bet: "why this exists — the opposite bet to the naive approach"
  what_it_is: "concise definition + capability table (tools / classes)"
  architecture: "mermaid flowchart of how it fits in the ecosystem"
  install: "bootstrap.sh (local, current) + future pip/PyPI note; per-client config if MCP"
  quickstart: "runnable example (code, CLI, or JSON-RPC) — copy-paste works"
  api: "key classes / functions with signatures + what they return"
  design_principles: "the rules it obeys (R9 no-silent-concession, negative-control, no-internal-leak, ...)"
  roadmap: "evolution plan — vX.Y with [x]/[ ] checkboxes (done / pending)"
  relationship: "how it composes with other vOS packages (esp. vsf-common, state-canon, socratic-engine)"
  measured: "claims measured not proclaimed (where a claim is made)"
  license: "Apache-2.0 (code) · CC-BY-4.0 (docs) — match state-canon-mcp convention"
}

enforcement() {
  scope: "ALL repos under ~/packages/{public,framework} AND the ~/vOSlab workspace"
  public_repos: "README.md is GitHub-facing (markdown); diagrams in mermaid"
  private_repos: "same sections; public face = README.md (markdown), internal canon may stay .vsm"
  gate: "P0.1 gate-suite SHOULD assert a README exists with these sections before a package is admitted"
  evolution: "every README carries a ROADMAP so the plan de evolucion is explicit per package"
}
⟦ /vos_package_readme_standard ⟧

⟦ /vos_package_readme_standard ⟧
